    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρῐκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεύς</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for a mule,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. ζεῦγος</span> a pair <i>of mules,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ly.</u>
				208b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				5.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.111
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.72a
			</span></i> :—the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεικός</span> occurs in Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.253
			</span></i> R. and <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> (interpol.) and as v.l. in Pl.l.c.</div>
